    {
      "id": "fr-child",
      "title": "Children 8–12 who can already read and write",
      "learner": "Children aged 8–12 who read and write confidently in their first language (English or another alphabetic language, or Chinese with pinyin); 2–3 lessons a week at school or in a club; short attention spans, motivated by games, songs and stories",
      "goal": "Reach A1 and a selected part of A2: talk about themselves, family, school, likes, food and holidays; read and write short texts; tell a simple story in the past",
      "entry": "Starts with classroom language, greetings and the sounds of French through songs and sound games before any grammar; the alphabet and sound–spelling links come early because children can already read",
      "assumes": null,
      "adapt": "No grammar terminology in instructions; grammar points are taught as patterns and chunks. Adult-oriented KCs (work, money, formal letters, complaints, the press, telephone etiquette) are left out; topics are re-skinned for school, pets, games and family. Mastery mainly via match, listen-comprehend, role-play and picture-based situated production. Required prerequisites of selected A2 points are pulled into the stage automatically.",
      "stages": [
        {
          "id": "child-1",
          "title": "Hello and the sounds of French",
          "band": "Stage 1",
          "kcs": [
