    {
      "id": "fr-adult-travel",
      "title": "Adults: everyday life and travel",
      "learner": "Adults (18+) learning for travel, a stay in a francophone country or social contact; limited time (1–3 hours a week), want usable language quickly and dislike long grammar explanations",
      "goal": "Handle travel and everyday transactions at A1, then solve problems (phone, complaints, health, services) and hold everyday conversations at A2",
      "entry": "Survival chunks first (greetings, spelling, numbers, personal details), then the transactional KCs of travel (shopping, restaurant, directions, transport, notices) are pulled forward before the rest of A1; each pulled KC brings its required prerequisites with it",
      "assumes": null,
      "adapt": "Grammar is introduced when a transaction needs it; mastery stresses role-play, listen-comprehend and real-document reading. School-oriented KCs, literary reading, the press, A2 pronoun subtleties (possessive/demonstrative/indefinite pronouns) and il faut que + subjunctive are left out of the core track.",
